;===========================================================
; 01c_params_kennedy.fis
;
; EXTERNAL VALIDATION parameter set for:
;   Kennedy, A.G.R., Jhuo, Y.S. & Ge, L. (2023)
;   "A laboratory investigation of using enzyme induced
;    calcite precipitation for soil strength improvement"
;   Smart Geotechnics for Smart Societies, Taylor & Francis,
;   pp. 572-577. DOI 10.1201/9781003299127-72 (Open Access)
;
; SEPARATE from 01_parameters.fis. That file holds the
; Gai & Sanchez (2019) verification set and is NOT touched.
; Never call both files in the same FLAC session - the second
; would silently overwrite the first.
;
; Soil: crushed silica sand (Singapore), Dr = 50 %
;   Cu = 1.403, Cc = 0.977, Gs = 2.66
;   emax = 0.911, emin = 0.574
;   e0 = 0.911 - 0.5(0.911 - 0.574) = 0.7425
;
; VARIABLE NAMING - IMPORTANT
; The names below are the ones 02_m_eicp.fis actually reads.
; They are NOT free to rename. The requested labels are given
; in comments where they differ:
;   $kappa_p  requested as $kappa
;   $lambda_p requested as $lambda
;   $m_cs     requested as $M_cs
;   $ds_p     requested as $Ds_p
;   $ini_e    requested as $ini_e0
; Using the requested spellings would leave the UDM globals
; undefined and the model would run on undefined values.
;===========================================================
;
def eicp_par_ken
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; HOST SAND PARAMETERS
;
; DECLARED ASSUMPTION: kappa, lambda, nu, Ds and eta are NOT
; measured by Kennedy et al. (2023) - no isotropic compression
; test is reported. They are carried over unchanged from Gai &
; Sanchez (2019) Table 1 (Ottawa sand). This is the principal
; caveat on the whole external validation and must be declared
; as an assumption, not presented as a calibrated value.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $kappa_p  = 0.003        ; assumed from Gai (no iso comp test)
    $lambda_p = 0.25         ; assumed from Gai (no iso comp test)
    $ds_p     = 0.04         ; assumed from Gai
    $nu_p     = 0.17         ; assumed from Gai
    $eta_p    = 60.0         ; assumed from Gai
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; CRITICAL STATE SLOPE - M MISMATCH DECLARED
;
; Kennedy et al. report, for PURE SAND, c'_res = 0 and
; phi'_res = 34.43 deg. With c' = 0 that IS the critical state
; friction angle, giving
;     M = 6 sin(34.43) / (3 - sin(34.43)) = 1.393
;
; The value used here is 1.09, the Gai & Sanchez Ottawa sand
; value. This is DELIBERATE. The mismatch (1.09 vs 1.393) is a
; SAND-TRANSFERABILITY FINDING to be reported, not corrected.
; Ottawa sand is rounded; this sand is crushed and angular, so
; a higher critical state friction angle is expected.
;
; CONSEQUENCE TO ANTICIPATE: the model's critical state
; asymptote is q = M p'. On the drained path p' = sigma3 + q/3
; this solves to q_crit = M sigma3 / (1 - M/3), giving
;
;   M = 1.09   ->  q_crit =  85.6 / 171.2 / 342.4 kPa
;   M = 1.393  ->  q_crit = 130.0 / 260.1 / 520.1 kPa
;                            (at sigma3 = 50 / 100 / 200 kPa)
;
; The residual strengths will therefore be UNDER-predicted by
; about 34 % at every confinement, BY CONSTRUCTION. That is
; the arithmetic consequence of the declared mismatch, not a
; defect, and it is a fixed ratio independent of pc, a or mu.
;
; DO NOT CHANGE M.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $m_cs     = 1.09         ; Gai & Sanchez value - see above
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; CEMENTATION PARAMETERS - APPLIED BLIND
;
; Published Gai & Sanchez (2019) Table 2 values, calibrated on
; MICP-treated Ottawa sand, applied here to EICP-treated
; crushed silica sand WITHOUT recalibration. Whether they
; transfer is the research question of this validation.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $a_pa     = 200000.0     ; bonding constant a, 200 kPa
    $mu_p     = 6.5          ; cementation damage rate, mu
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; INITIAL STATE - Kennedy sand
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $ini_e    = 0.7425       ; void ratio at Dr = 50 %
    $ini_r    = 0.01         ; fallback only; ini_eicp_r
;                              recomputes R0 from the stresses
    $ini_chi  = 1.0          ; intact bonding at t = 0
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; PRE-CONSOLIDATION PRESSURE - CALIBRATION TRIAL LOG
;
; pc is calibrated against the PURE SAND peak at sigma3 =
; 200 kPa (Kennedy Table 1: q = 629.11 kPa at 3-5 % strain).
;
; ---- TRIAL 1: 7,476,000 Pa - REJECTED ----
; Derived in closed form from the surface-size requirement:
;   p'        = 200 + 629.11/3                = 409.703 kPa
;   q^2/M^2   = 395779.39 / 1.1881            = 333119.6
;   p'^2                                       = 167856.8
;   p0_needed = (333119.6 + 167856.8)/409.703 = 1222.78 kPa
;   R0        = 200 / 1222.78                 = 0.16356
;   pc        = 1222.78 / 0.16356             = 7476 kPa
;
; RESULT: peak q = 2440 kPa at 2.4 % axial strain, against a
; target of 629 kPa at 3-5 %. Overshoot factor 3.9, and the
; peak arrived too early. Run confirmed R0 = 0.026, pb = 0
; throughout, pc falling 7500 -> 1440 kPa (correct direction),
; unbalanced force zero. The model behaved correctly; the
; input value was wrong.
;
; WHY IT FAILED: the derivation is not self-consistent. It
; takes R0 from p0_needed and then recovers pc as
; p0_needed/R0, which reduces to pc = p0_needed^2 / sigma3.
; Substituting pc = 7476 kPa back into the model's own
; consistent initialisation gives R0 = 200/7476 = 0.027, not
; the 0.164 the derivation assumed - and the run measured
; 0.026. More generally, NO closed-form route from a target
; peak to pc exists: R, pc, chi and the dilation response
; evolve in a coupled way during shearing, the same coupling
; demonstrated in both parameter directions during the Gai
; mu and a sensitivity studies.
;
; ---- TRIAL 2: 1,350,000 Pa - CURRENT ----
; Estimated empirically by scaling the verified Gai & Sanchez
; pc calibration rather than by closed form:
;   Gai Ottawa sand at sigma3 = 200 kPa:
;     pc = 800 kPa -> pure sand peak 420 kPa
;     pc = 900 kPa -> pure sand peak 460 kPa
;     i.e. about 0.4 kPa of peak per kPa of pc
;   Direct proportion: 800 x (629/420)         = 1198 kPa
;   Allowing for the sublinear pc/pb compensation the
;   plausible bracket is roughly 1200-1500 kPa.
; Set at 1350 kPa, mid-bracket.
;
; ACCEPTANCE CRITERION: peak q = 629 +/- 15 kPa at 3-5 %
; axial strain. Judge BOTH magnitude AND strain-to-peak.
; Trial 1 failed on both. Matching the peak magnitude at the
; wrong strain would point at eta, not pc.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $ini_pc_ken = 1350000.0  ; TRIAL 2 (Pa)
    $ini_pc     = 1350000.0  ; UDM fallback, keep equal to above
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; NUMERICAL GUARDS - identical to the verified Gai set
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $p_min    = 1.0          ; floor on mean effective stress
    $pc_min   = 100.0        ; floor on pre-consolidation press.
    $chi_min  = 1.0e-6       ; floor on damage factor
    $r_min    = 1.0e-6       ; floor on sub-loading ratio
    $r_max    = 1.0          ; ceiling on sub-loading ratio
    $kb_dflt  = 1.0e10       ; default bulk modulus bound (Pa)
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; SUBZONE ACCUMULATORS - volume weighted, reset each zsub cycle
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $m_wt_acc   = 0.0        ; accumulated subzone volume
    $m_vol_acc  = 0.0        ; total volumetric strain
    $m_depv_acc = 0.0        ; plastic volumetric strain
    $m_depq_acc = 0.0        ; plastic deviatoric strain
    $m_dept_acc = 0.0        ; plastic strain norm
    $m_p_acc    = 0.0        ; mean effective stress
    $m_q_acc    = 0.0        ; deviatoric stress
    $m_pls_acc  = 0.0        ; plasticity flag
;
end
;
eicp_par_ken
;
;===========================================================
; EOF
;===========================================================
